{
  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2023_W31_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-31",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2023_W31_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-31.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2023-08-04",
  "report_week": "31",
  "report_period": "Week 31 (28th Jul to 4th Aug 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Kitaura Kaiun have committed their Capesize \"Shiosai\" 176/2009 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 07/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese buyers for USD 20,85 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older \"Ocean Cobalt\" 180/2008 Imabari, Japan (SS 07/2028, DD 04/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold in July at USD 19,5 mill. The Panamax \"Despina D\" 76/2004 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 10/2024, BWTS fitted) from Oinoussian Diamond Shipping was committed to undisclosed buyers for mid-high USD 10 mill. Remind you that back in April, the \"Navios Anthos\" 75/2004 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 11,25 mill. On the Supramax sector, Deval Shipping & Trading committed their \"Devbulk Gulten\" 55/2015 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) for USD 22,6 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Nord Treasure\" 55/2014 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 21,7 mill. The OHBS Handysize \"Cielo Di Palermo\" 37/2013 Saiki, Japan (SS 08/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 17 mill. Remind you that the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Maestro Diamond\" 37/2015 Saiki, Japan (SS 05/2025, DD 05/2023) was sold back in May at USD 22,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "Oman Shipping have committed their VLCC sister vessels \"Fida\" & \"Sifa\" 316/2011 Hyundai, Korea (SS 05/2026, DD 05/2024 & SS 01/2026, DD 02/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted both) and their Japanese built \"Saham\" 300/2010 Universal, Japan (SS 10/2025, DD 12/2023, Scrubber fitted) to Korean buyers Sinokor for USD 64 mill each. Remind you that the \"Astro Chloe\" 318/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 01/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold in July at region USD 62,5 mill. The Aframax \"Tornado A\" 105/2003 Sumitomo, Japan (SS 09/2025, DD 10/2023) was committed to undisclosed buyers for USD 24,75 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger \"Sea Hazel\" 106/2004 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 01/2024, DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in May at excess USD 31 mill. Viken Shipping have sold the MR2 \"Cassiopeia II\" 50/2008 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 10/2023, BWTS fitted) to Far Eastern buyers for USD 23 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Elandra Corallo\" 50/2008 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 10/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold recently at the same price.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low usd 8,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 8,000/10,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 7,000/9.000 pd. Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 5,000/6,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via South America were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 20,000/22,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K/600K. A Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 9,550 pd basis delivery China for 6/9 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 8,000/10,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 9,000/10,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 200K. Indian Coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Indian trips into Japan were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. An Ultramax was fixed on period at the usd 14,000 pd basis delivery South East Asia for 3/5 months employment.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from China into South Africa were reported at the level of usd 6,000/7,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 7,000/9.000 pd. Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 8,000/9,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
